#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:5
#: 692f27ee7bff49f3b7b959b073fc31ba
msgid "Object Avoidance with Bendy Ruler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:10
#: ac5d94851c9d475eb68b4d2fc8dbf9d4
msgid "Copter and Rover support \"BendyRuler\" for path planning around obstacles and fences.  The BendyRuler algorithm probes around the vehicle in many directions looking for open spaces and then tries to pick the direction that is sufficiently open while also moving the vehicle towards the final destination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:14
#: f9bbbd741e2644dca74d4afece562f7f
msgid "This is only applicable in AUTO, GUIDED, and RTL flight modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:20
#: dfae4880233a478f9f11b7e8642d2473
msgid "Basic Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:22
#: 6cf0abba276647b79546937711334ccc
msgid ":ref:`OA_TYPE <OA_TYPE>` = 1 (BendyRuler).  You may need to refresh parameters after changing this to see the parameters below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:23
#: 1bae6face0e84b83aa52ea301550cf59
msgid ":ref:`OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD <OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD>`: This parameter is called \"OA_LOOKAHEAD\" before Copter and Rover 4.1. It is the distance (in meters) ahead of the vehicle that should be probed.  Obstacles further than this far away will be ignored.  This should be long enough that the path around obstacles can be \"seen\" but not too long or the vehicle will be overly cautious and not enter areas with a lot of obstacles. 5m is typical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:24
#: 1164a07cfaa14931a06b196db11a7df7
msgid ":ref:`OA_MARGIN_MAX <OA_MARGIN_MAX>`: the distance (in meters) that the vehicle should stay away from obstacles. 2m is a typical value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:28
#: f5ea39d3c6a343c98c4fe849fc3fe2a5
msgid "Users often get confused between OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD and OA_MARGIN_MAX parameters. A smaller OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD will make BendyRuler look for obstacles in a shorter path towards the destination, and thus any object further than this many meters will not be used in the path planning process. A shorter OA_MARGIN_MAX parameter will let the vehicle come closer to an approaching obstacle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:31
#: 0cca9cd292294030a4f7edabbc46c785
msgid "BendyRuler Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:33
#: 163b0c73aa354ff2bfa430d7c4e590b3
msgid "Copter 4.1 onwards has support for two different types of BendyRuler Path Planning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:35
#: e260b31309bf46528f3be728998eda2f
msgid ":ref:`OA_BR_TYPE <OA_BR_TYPE>` = 1: Horizontal BendyRuler: This is the only option available on Rover and older Copter versions. This searches for obstacle-free paths only in horizontal directions and therefore when it detects an obstacle in its path, it will only move in those directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:42
#: 502a8de5d21a446cbaa64201cac5452b
msgid ":ref:`OA_BR_TYPE <OA_BR_TYPE>` = 2: Vertical BendyRuler: This feature searches for path only in four directions: Straight towards the destination, vertically up, vertically down and backwards. This feature is typically helpful while avoiding short obstacles in a crowded space. Don't forget to setup an altitude fence if you do not want the Copter to climb above a certain height."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:49
#: e187e4a8f77b4d1b8f6f4b5551bf51d2
msgid "Advanced Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:51
#: 731333fe6f3642e8801172789d9e6590
msgid "If using a lidar or proximity sensor the following \"obstacle database\" parameters are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:53
#: 523ee528659a4e53a0ed24d3e2f9739c
msgid ":ref:`OA_DB_SIZE <OA_DB_SIZE>`: the maximum number of obstacles that can be tracked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:54
#: c6b4eadae4e54f3cbc945fa1ae3275d1
msgid ":ref:`OA_DB_EXPIRE <OA_DB_EXPIRE>`: the number of seconds after an obstacle disappears from view that it is removed from the database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:55
#: 52e95a3595ca453e8113a637e8f6d945
msgid ":ref:`OA_DB_QUEUE_SIZE <OA_DB_QUEUE_SIZE>`: the buffer size between the lidar and obstacle database.  Normally this can be left at the default value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:56
#: 4658b40004844dec829b0d9830744c2c
msgid ":ref:`OA_DB_OUTPUT <OA_DB_OUTPUT>`: controls whether tracked objects are visible on the GCS as small airplanes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oa-bendyruler.rst:57
#: 6001f4495892414187e5ca0706fc401e
msgid ":ref:`OA_DB_ALT_MIN <OA_DB_ALT_MIN>`: OADatabase will reject obstacle's if vehicle's altitude above home is below this parameter, in a 3 meter radius around home. This can be useful if your sensor is picking up the ground as obstacles while taking off."
msgstr ""

